WEBVTT

00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:04.952
-(SCREAMING)
-(CRASHING)

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:07.512
SIMULATOR: You have crashed.
You have crashed.

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:10.032
-Are you all right?
-You have crashed.

00:00:10.592 --> 00:00:11.712
I have crashed.

00:00:11.752 --> 00:00:12.832
(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)

00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:14.432
(POWER SHUTS DOWN)

00:00:17.992 --> 00:00:19.872
CRUZ: It's not easy for him.
STERLING: Cruz, just relax.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:21.512
-Give him another chance.
-STERLING: I will talk to him.

00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:24.712
CRUZ: I can still work with him.
STERLING: I know he's your project.

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:26.192
-CRUZ: Are you sure?
-Cruz.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.592
-CRUZ: Well, can't you just--
-Cruz.

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:28.792
CRUZ: It's not easy for him.

00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:30.592
STERLING: Look, I'm trying to help you.
McQUEEN: Whoa.

00:00:31.632 --> 00:00:33.432
You're all warshed up, McQueen.

00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:35.232
(STUTTERS) I'm sorry. What?

00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:38.992
I said, the floor's
all washed up and clean.

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:41.352
Oh, right. (CHUCKLES)

00:00:41.432 --> 00:00:43.272
-STERLING: Thank you very much.
-Uh...

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:45.312
Good luck.

00:00:46.272 --> 00:00:47.832
STERLING: Hey, Lightning.

00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:50.632
Come on in.
Got something to show you. You ready?

00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:52.312
Uh, for what?

00:00:54.952 --> 00:00:56.232
Wow.

00:00:58.112 --> 00:01:01.032
You are about to become
the biggest brand in racing.

00:01:01.232 --> 00:01:05.352
We are talking saturation on all
continents for every demographic.

00:01:05.512 --> 00:01:08.632
Movie deals, infomercials,
product endorsements.

00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:11.192
-McQUEEN: Mudflaps?
-Of course.

00:01:11.312 --> 00:01:14.232
We'll be rich beyond belief.
You think you're famous now?

00:01:14.312 --> 00:01:15.312
-(LAUGHS)
-(CHUCKLES SHEEPISHLY)

00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:18.312
I thought you'd be mad
about the simulator.

00:01:18.472 --> 00:01:21.672
I mean, this is all great, Mr. Sterling,
I guess, but I don't know.

00:01:21.872 --> 00:01:23.992
I've never really thought
of myself as a brand.

00:01:24.472 --> 00:01:27.872
Oh, nor do I. I'm a fan.
Maybe your most avid.

00:01:27.952 --> 00:01:30.152
I think of this as your legacy!

00:01:31.432 --> 00:01:32.592
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:01:32.832 --> 00:01:35.992
It sounds like something that
happens after you're done racing.

00:01:39.352 --> 00:01:40.872
Mr. Sterling, what is this about?

00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:44.512
Look, Lightning. I'm not gonna race you.

00:01:44.832 --> 00:01:46.912
What? What do you mean not race me?

00:01:47.192 --> 00:01:49.352
-Hold on. Hold on.
-I'm not going to Florida?

00:01:49.512 --> 00:01:54.712
You have no idea how excited I was
to get you here because...

00:01:54.792 --> 00:01:57.472
I knew you'd be back.

00:01:58.192 --> 00:02:00.192
It was gonna be the
comeback story of the year!

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:04.792
But your speed and performance
just aren't where they need to be.

00:02:05.392 --> 00:02:06.392
I'm sorry.

00:02:06.712 --> 00:02:10.232
We're talking about speed
on a simulator.

00:02:10.392 --> 00:02:12.752
-Listen to how crazy that sounds.
-Look, I'm trying to help you.

00:02:12.912 --> 00:02:16.112
As your sponsor, yes,
but also as your friend.

00:02:16.272 --> 00:02:19.392
Your racing days are coming to an end.

00:02:19.552 --> 00:02:22.312
Every time you lose,
you damage yourself.

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:24.672
Damage the brand, you mean?

00:02:25.272 --> 00:02:28.152
Oh, Lightning, come on.
You've done the work.

00:02:28.232 --> 00:02:31.392
Now move on to the next phase
and reap the reward.

00:02:31.872 --> 00:02:35.112
The racing is the reward. Not the stuff.

00:02:35.712 --> 00:02:36.992
I don't want to cash in.

00:02:37.152 --> 00:02:39.392
I want to feel the rush
of moving 200 miles an hour...

00:02:39.552 --> 00:02:40.872
inches from the other guys,

00:02:40.912 --> 00:02:42.712
pushing myself faster
than I thought I could go!

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:45.312
That's the reward, Mr. Sterling!

00:02:46.272 --> 00:02:47.312
Oh, Lightning, come on.

00:02:49.152 --> 00:02:52.352
Look, I can do this. I can, I promise!

00:02:52.392 --> 00:02:54.072
I'll train like I did with Doc.

00:02:54.232 --> 00:02:57.472
I'll get my tires dirty
on every dirt track from here to Florida.

00:02:58.752 --> 00:03:01.592
I can start on Fireball Beach
where all the old greats used to race.

00:03:02.232 --> 00:03:03.712
Get your tires dirty.

00:03:03.992 --> 00:03:05.912
That's how you're gonna
get faster than Storm?

00:03:06.072 --> 00:03:09.752
Yes! Exactly! I mean, sacred dirt, right?

00:03:10.952 --> 00:03:14.752
Mr. Sterling, if you care about
my legacy, the one that Doc started,

00:03:14.952 --> 00:03:18.312
you'll let me do this.
I promise you, I will win.

00:03:18.992 --> 00:03:21.832
(SIGHS) I don't know.
What you're asking, it's too risky.

00:03:22.112 --> 00:03:24.992
Come on. You like it, I can tell.

00:03:25.112 --> 00:03:29.192
It's got that little "comeback story
of the year" feel to it, doesn't it?

00:03:31.272 --> 00:03:32.472
(SIGHS)

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:34.552
One race?

00:03:37.272 --> 00:03:39.432
If you don't win at Florida,
you'll retire?

00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:42.712
Look, if I don't win
I'll sell all the mudflaps you got.

00:03:42.872 --> 00:03:47.632
But if I do win,
I decide when I'm done. Deal?

00:03:49.512 --> 00:03:50.512
Deal.

00:03:51.152 --> 00:03:53.872
Thank you, Mr. Sterling.
You won't be sorry.

00:03:54.072 --> 00:03:57.192
Just one thing and this is only because
I don't like taking chances.

00:03:57.352 --> 00:03:59.192
You're taking someone with you.

00:04:01.592 --> 00:04:02.872
(CRUZ PANTING)

00:04:03.992 --> 00:04:04.992
(GRUNTING)

00:04:05.752 --> 00:04:06.952
(PANTING)

00:04:06.992 --> 00:04:09.832
You talked him into it!
Way to go, Mr. McQueen!

00:04:09.992 --> 00:04:11.472
(SIGHS) Cruz.

00:04:11.872 --> 00:04:14.472
You could talk a snowmobile
into an air conditioner.

00:04:14.912 --> 00:04:16.992
You're going with me? With that thing?

00:04:17.192 --> 00:04:21.672
Yeah. You still need my help.
You're brittle like a fossil.

00:04:21.992 --> 00:04:23.392
(WHIRRING)

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:30.032
-We got the cable. (MUMBLING)
-I don't need a trainer out here, Cruz.

00:04:30.672 --> 00:04:31.912
You're old!

00:04:31.992 --> 00:04:33.672
What if you fall on this beach
and can't get up?

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:37.192
Well, life's a beach and then you drive.

00:04:38.272 --> 00:04:39.512
(LAUGHS)

00:04:39.552 --> 00:04:41.232
-Oh, McQueen.
-Thank you.

00:04:41.512 --> 00:04:43.272
This is beautiful.

00:04:43.512 --> 00:04:46.192
I can see why Mr. Sterling
said you wanted to train here.

00:04:46.872 --> 00:04:48.192
As soon as this thing's booted up,

00:04:48.272 --> 00:04:50.632
we'll get you on the treadmill...
and I'll track your speed.

00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:51.952
What? No!

00:04:52.032 --> 00:04:55.712
The whole idea is getting
my tires dirty. Real racing.

00:04:55.872 --> 00:04:57.152
I'm not driving on that thing

00:04:57.192 --> 00:04:59.352
when I've got the sand
and the whole earth.

00:04:59.952 --> 00:05:01.032
(MACHINE CHIMING)

00:05:01.072 --> 00:05:04.192
-Oh, okay.
-Luigi, let's do this.

00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:07.192
LUIGI: Welcome, racers,
to Fireball Beach!

00:05:07.392 --> 00:05:11.072
Historic home for today's
great test of speed.

00:05:11.272 --> 00:05:15.232
Our finish line will be
the abandoned pier in the distance.

00:05:15.712 --> 00:05:20.592
All right. Quicker than quick,
faster than fast, I am speed--

00:05:20.752 --> 00:05:24.232
That is great self-motivation.
Did you come up with that?

00:05:24.312 --> 00:05:25.392
Yeah, I did.

00:05:25.432 --> 00:05:28.712
On your mark. Get set. Go!

